{
 "_about": [
  "The rule IDs of the secret scanners envdrift grades by rule, one sorted list per tool.",
  "tests/scanner/test_severity_policy.py checks them against the shared rule table, so a",
  "provider whose credential rules the table forgot cannot fall back to HIGH by mistake.",
  "This is a snapshot: it does not follow a tool upgrade by itself. When a pinned tool is",
  "bumped (src/envdrift/constants.json), extract the lists again and grade any new rule.",
  "gitleaks and Infisical: every 'id = \"...\"' line of the rules embedded in the binary.",
  "The snapshot was taken from gitleaks 8.30.1 (the pin when it was taken), Infisical 0.43.135",
  "(the gitleaks engine) and Infisical 0.43.141 (the betterleaks engine). Extract them with a",
  "regular expression over the binary:",
  "re.findall(rb'(?m)^id\\s*=\\s*\"([a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]*)\"', open(binary, 'rb').read()).",
  "kingfisher: the 'Rule ID' column of https://mongodb.github.io/kingfisher/rules/builtin-rules/.",
  "Its 'betterleaks.<id>' rules are betterleaks' rules under the same <id>."
 ],
